"""
bookify — render any folder's docs as a browsable book (HTML + Markdown).

Walks a directory tree, collects documentation files (Markdown/MDX, rst, HTML,
txt, adoc — and optionally source code), and generates:

  <out>/html/      a static HTML book with a sidebar navigation tree,
                   per-page prev/next links, and syntax highlighting
  <out>/markdown/  a Markdown book: SUMMARY.md (table of contents),
                   normalized per-file pages, and BOOK.md (single combined file)

Output goes to ~/.cache/bookify/<name>-<pathhash>/ by default, NOT into the
scanned folder, so rendered artifacts never pollute a repo. Every output dir
also gets a `.gitignore` containing `*` as a safety net for custom -o paths.

Usage:
  bookify <folder> [-o OUT] [--format html|md|both] [--title TITLE]
                   [--include-code] [--serve [PORT]] [--no-serve]

By default bookify builds and then serves the HTML book locally (opening the
browser). Pass --no-serve for a build-only run (e.g. from scripts or agents).
"""

